# N3: the whole route to a live match, then a post-goal auto replay sampled by
# the engine's own state lines instead of by predicted frames.
#
# Three engine lines make the post-goal sequence observable:
#   [match] t=... state=2 .....  GS_POST_GOAL, the match's own goal detection, printed once a
#                                second while the sim runs
#   [task] state=0x100 ........  presentation/NIS, entered for the goal celebration
#   [task] state=0x10 .........  the port's own name for the auto-replay task state,
#                                printed on entry and about every 120 frames while it holds
# The control heartbeat is 600 frames, longer than the replay itself, so a frame-anchored
# sample could miss the replay entirely.  Each wait-log consumes the line it matched, so
# repeating a wait walks through the later occurrences of a periodic line.
#
# Goal timing is not reproducible run to run (observed first goals at match t=11.0, t=10.9 and
# t~78), so the scenario predicts no frame: it arms a wait while the match is still goalless and
# lets the match score when it scores.  The arming point is the first live-play line, which the
# [match] line announces as state=4.  That line carries t= and ball= fields between the tag and
# the state, so a needle must not jump straight from "[match]" to "state="; written that way it
# matches nothing and the wait stalls until its timeout.
# Nothing is injected here.  The goal is whatever the match scores on its own, and the match's
# own detection, celebration script, scorer credit and auto replay follow from it.  If a run ever
# plays a goal-less match the port has a fallback in its own debug channel (PDBG_WARP_BALL, op 8)
# -- the same request the debug menu's "into home net" button sends.
#
# health -> saving/loading -> legal -> intro movie -> title -> main menu -> mariobg ->
# choose captains (both sides) -> stadium select -> loading -> live match -> goal ->
# goal presentation -> auto replay -> kickoff.
env STRIKERS_LOG_SCENES=1
env STRIKERS_LOG_MATCH=1
env STRIKERS_LOG_NIS=1
env STRIKERS_AUTOPRESS=A@s51+180,A@s2+240,A@s53+120,A@s3+240,A@s8+300,A@s8+420,A@s8+540,A@s8+660,LEFT@s8+780,A@s8+900,A@s8+1020,A@s9+300
require-scene choose_captains
wait-log state=4 ot=0 score @420
shot kickoff
dump kickoff
wait-log state=2 ot=0 @540
shot goal
dump postgoal
wait-log [task] state=0x100 renderWorld @240
shot goal_pres
dump goal_pres
wait-log [task] state=0x10 renderWorld @180
shot replay0
dump replay0
wait-log [task] state=0x10 renderWorld @120
shot replay1
dump replay1
wait-log [task] state=0x10 renderWorld @120
shot replay2
dump replay2
wait-log [task] state=0x10 renderWorld @120
shot replay3
dump replay3
wait-log [task] state=0x2 renderWorld @180
shot back_to_play
dump back_to_play
require-frame 9000
dump middlegame
expect [task] state=0x10 renderWorld
expect [task] state=0x100 renderWorld
expect state=2 ot=0
